{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DESIGN DECISION (operator-ratified 2026-08-22), recorded before implementation per protocol:\n\n- IMPLEMENT ONLY option (a): call-local deduplication of OpenGrep configuration validation within a single plan-review/scan invocation (one `semgrep --validate --config <source>` per unique detector source_path per `_run_opengrep` call, result fanned out to every detector from that source). This is pure waste-removal — no behavior change, no boundary change, no persistent or cross-scan caching. Scan execution, output normalization, coverage records, and all unique external-boundary tests stay unchanged.\n- DO NOT implement option (b), cross-worker scan-result reuse. It will be FILED as a separate `idea` ticket linked `discovered_from` this ticket, capturing the caching-boundary design question: stale-result risk if the tree changes mid-run, and the unsolved cross-worker sharing under pytest-xdist (`-n 3 --dist worksteal` fixtures are worker-local).\n- The gw0-crash datum from the earlier observation comment (test_opengrep_timeout_via_harness worker crash, one local occurrence, not reproduced) is already covered by the CI-timeout lane — no separate ticket will be filed for it here.\n\nThe ticket description will be aligned with this ratified implementation scope (the original research-only ACs 'no production code or test files change' / 'no scanner invocation removed or mocked' are superseded by the operator ratification for option (a); no scanner invocation is removed or mocked by option (a) either — only duplicate validation subprocesses are eliminated)."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787437777656269001,"uuid":"2dfb6950-e109-438c-9dd2-d7f335bc7856"}